{"id": "86152", "name": "צמצום שבר אלגברי – v/(av) (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Simplify the following algebraic fractions:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{{CT:0}}{{CT:1}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Cancel the common factor</b><br>Write the numerator as a product too: <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:0}}=1\\cdot {{CT:0}}\\)</span>. The factor <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:0}}\\)</span> is common to the top and the bottom (we assume it is not zero), so it cancels:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{{CT:0}}{{CT:1}}=\\frac{1\\cdot {{CT:0}}}{{{CT:2}}\\cdot {{CT:0}}} \\]</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{{CT:0}}{{CT:1}} = {{CT:3}}. \\]</p>The important thing is that you remember that <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\frac{{CT:0}}{{CT:0}} = 1\\)</span> and so the top of the fraction does not cancel to <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(0\\)</span>.</div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": false, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "EqualComAss", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "1-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer is algebraically equivalent to the correct answer but you haven't simplified fully.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "1-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-2-T (cancelling a/a to 0)", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">It looks like you have cancelled the top of the fraction to 0 but remember that \\(\\frac{{CT:0}}{{CT:0}} = 1\\) not 0</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-2-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["a", "ta", "v"], "nvariants": 6}